#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:5
#: 89161aefb9224e0095a90cb78343809c
msgid "ArduPilot Developer Code of Conduct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:6
#: 2d1d7f957c54418183a01964f51534a9
msgid "Rev 1.0 Jan 2nd 2018"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:9
#: e8acac2eae534f4ab862232da2aed4b0
msgid "Our Aim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:11
#: 0a9d32bfc7c04fbbb15a719efcd71c5f
msgid "ArduPilot aims to enable the creation and use of trusted, autonomous, unmanned vehicle systems for the peaceful benefit of all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:14
#: a31a3c71c75841ec913d183049dbb804
msgid "Our Team"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:16
#: 3c134e6f90b7483587bee44e9ecc63de
msgid "The ArduPilot team is global.  It consists of the Development Team plus many contributors, from many fields and many places.  By choosing to be part of the ArduPilot Development Team, you choose to accept this Code of Conduct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:19
#: 35eca082e932430dbfcbf23e9fedc255
msgid "Our Pledge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:21
#: 7b20bce3504f4365854ad597aab1262a
msgid "In the interest of fostering an open and welcoming environment, we as developers and maintainers pledge to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:23
#: c860383458a44037af63ea08ab92bb3d
msgid "Endeavour to make participation in our project and our community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, disability, ethnicity, gender identity and expression, level of experience, nationality, personal appearance, race, religion, or sexual identity and orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:24
#: 6c9efe201eba42818ac4c3f8b6b4a89b
msgid "Endeavour to understand the intent of development activities they undertake, where there may be reason to think that the vehicle may be used as a weapon or in an application where it is effectively in control of human life."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:25
#: a0d8a17f827d4d8494f6eee3358e8dc6
msgid "Not knowingly support or facilitate the weaponization of systems using ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:26
#: 4c136da690c9425c95cd609d4f93c1a3
msgid "ArduPilot is NOT certified for use in applications where ArduPilot is effectively in control of human lives. Members of the development team must not knowingly assist in projects where ArduPilot will be in control of human lives.  “In control of human lives” includes but isn’t limited to manned aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:29
#: 151a2bcc4ef6415b95a2689712d24561
msgid "Our Standards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:31
#: c6dfbda3b0544450aa94ace669e63bbe
msgid "Examples of behavior that contributes to achieving the aims of ArduPilot include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:33
#: 397bf1bafc8c4fdb9c6e7c354ea98053
msgid "Using welcoming and inclusive language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:34
#: 7c879ff2cd5e4d2cb95fcbc06d159da2
msgid "Being respectful of differing viewpoints and experiences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:35
#: a19855fbf1be48b18ea42eb22773d495
msgid "Gracefully accepting constructive criticism"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:36
#: 69542de002ce451890d522df3f7a7c0c
msgid "Focusing on what is best for the community"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:37
#: 75ea4cadaf934b02946df1aebe509dce
msgid "Showing empathy towards other community members"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:39
#: 452a098d326a41d2a7265ddd98984c42
msgid "Examples of unacceptable behavior by contributors include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:41
#: bfc4143ab7684d91b155862b21cf3c67
msgid "The use of sexualized language or imagery and unwelcome sexual attention or advances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:42
#: 5d12743dd93e4ff2898320eb181d3868
msgid "Trolling, insulting/derogatory comments, and personal or political attacks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:43
#: 0a84786c59b0449184e4d5f13333ad28
msgid "Public or private harassment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:44
#: 4af24c0a1ddb48ab8bf6dc5684e58d72
msgid "Publishing others’ private information, such as a physical or electronic address, without explicit permission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:45
#: be3e57210bdc4c078a578c027c41ddcf
msgid "Modifying ArduPilot code to intentionally support weaponization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:46
#: f6ce40da18bb4eeca5c3ad005d0ac795
msgid "Knowingly designing, testing or using weaponized systems running ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:47
#: 780fa95b9391449fa7211bfe4c939f89
msgid "Other conduct which could reasonably be considered inappropriate in a public or professional setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:50
#: 11b622efeb934ff4a15d552289a279a5
msgid "Our Responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:52
#: c1b343658d9a4421b3102fb1e7648142
msgid "Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying the standards of acceptable behavior and are expected to take appropriate and fair corrective action in response to any instances of unacceptable behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:54
#: a54ca0a738ed42599813114422f2399a
msgid "Project maintainers have the right and responsibility to remove, edit, or reject comments, commits, code, wiki edits, issues, and other contributions that are not aligned to this Code of Conduct, or to ban temporarily or permanently any contributor for other behaviors that they deem inappropriate, threatening, offensive, or harmful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:57
#: 5a2dd4306d6949ba8a5a19444e45fea3
msgid "Scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:59
#: b5bb8cc0650a4cc58d477bdec67d5efd
msgid "This Code of Conduct applies both within project spaces and in public spaces when an individual is representing the ArduPilot project or its community. Examples of representing the ArduPilot project or community include using an official project e-mail address, posting via an official social media account, or acting as an appointed representative at an online or offline event. Representation of the ArduPilot project may be further defined and clarified by project maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:61
#: ca4b97218b914d4883823ac6ee32f3f5
msgid "In addition, the rules regarding weaponization and manned vehicles using ArduPilot apply regardless of whether you are representing the ArduPilot project at the time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:64
#: 4d341a33ed8e4d27adce867fc8e2f484
msgid "Enforcement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:65
#: 32aaa4874e6048838564adc683af592c
msgid "Instances of abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behavior, and other actions not consistent with this Code of Conduct may be reported by contacting the project team at ardupilot.devel@gmail.com. All complaints will be reviewed and investigated and will result in a response that is deemed necessary and appropriate to the circumstances. The project team is obligated to maintain confidentiality with regard to the reporter of an incident. Further details of specific enforcement policies may be posted separately. Project maintainers who do not follow or enforce the Code of Conduct in good faith may face temporary or permanent repercussions as determined by other members of the project’s leadership team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:69
#: 9d97290bde6844fbb4304b4b5e7b7ba2
msgid "Attribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/developer-code-of-conduct.rst:70
#: 908eaf4552574bffb5a5128ba63b5786
msgid "This Code of Conduct is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 1.4, available at https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/1/4/code-of-conduct.html"
msgstr ""
